#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Party-blind wording for every quiz statement.

The quiz must not tell the voter which party a statement belongs to, so each statement
describes a policy and what it would mean, with no party or leader names, no branded
bill or scheme names, and no "the government did X" framing. Party positions and their
evidence live in quiz_data.py and are only shown AFTER the voter has answered.

quiz_build.py applies these texts over quiz_data.py and refuses to build if any statement
still contains an identifying term (see BANNED in quiz_build.py).
"""

